<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carhaix-Plouguer</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Vorgium</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carhaix-Plouguer is a town in central Brittany, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finistere">Finistère</a>. Under Roman rule it was Vorgium, the capital of the Osismii, a planned town with a grid of streets, public baths and a long aqueduct. It lay at the meeting of several Roman roads across the Armorican peninsula and later became the main town of the Poher district.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carhaix-plouguer.jpg" alt="Carhaix-Plouguer" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moreau.henri · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carhaix_22_Maison_ancienne_devenue_syndicat_d%27initiative.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
